# Generate and update Anki decks from JSON

Canonical page: https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/json-to-anki/
Language: en
Description: Read JSON with Rust, Python or TypeScript, package images and audio, then review an answer-only APKG update.

Read three biology questions from JSON, add a shared image and audio clip, and export an original APKG plus a reviewed answer-only update. Each release should contain **3 notes, 3 cards and 2 media files**. Choose one SDK below; each is a complete program. Normal export needs no Anki installation.

Maintained by Anki Forge maintainers · reviewed 2026-10-25.

## Shared inputs

Download [v1.json](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/v1.json), [v2.json](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/v2.json), [cell.png](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/cell.png) and [tone.wav](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/tone.wav). The image is a cell diagram; the audio is a short generated tone, not spoken vocabulary. In each new application directory, put these four files in `recipe/`:

```text
json-deck/
  recipe/
    v1.json
    v2.json
    cell.png
    tone.wav
```

Both JSON files contain `namespace`, `deck` and three `notes` with durable `id`, `front` and `back` values. v2 changes only the first answer. The caller parses JSON; Anki Forge handles authoring and APKG generation. For untrusted inputs, validate your application’s schema before constructing notes.

## Rust

Rust 1.92+. JSON parsing uses `serde` and `serde_json`. Use public Anki Forge 0.3.1.

```sh
cargo new json-deck
cd json-deck
cargo add ankiforge@0.3.1
cargo add serde --features derive
cargo add serde_json
```

Save as `src/main.rs` (create `recipe/` alongside `Cargo.toml`):

```rust
use ankiforge::update::CompareOptions;
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Content, Media, Note, Project};
use serde::Deserialize;
use std::{fs, path::Path};

#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct Dataset {
    namespace: String,
    deck: String,
    notes: Vec<Row>,
}

#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct Row {
    id: String,
    front: String,
    back: String,
}

fn project(input: &Path, version: &str) -> Result<Project, Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let data: Dataset = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(input.join(version))?)?;
    let image = Media::file(input.join("cell.png"))?;
    let audio = Media::file(input.join("tone.wav"))?;
    let mut project = Project::new(data.namespace)?.default_deck(data.deck);
    for row in data.notes {
        let front = Content::sequence([Content::text(row.front), image.image(), audio.sound()]);
        project.add(row.id, Note::basic(front, row.back))?;
    }
    Ok(project)
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let args: Vec<_> = std::env::args().collect();
    let input = Path::new(args.get(1).map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("recipe"));
    let output = Path::new(args.get(2).map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("output/rust"));
    fs::create_dir_all(output)?;
    let baseline = output.join("v1.apkg");
    let candidate = output.join("v2.apkg");
    if baseline.exists() || candidate.exists() {
        return Err("Choose a fresh output directory; keep original releases".into());
    }
    project(input, "v1.json")?.build(BuildOptions::to(&baseline))?;
    let next = project(input, "v2.json")?;
    let comparison = next.compare(CompareOptions::against(&baseline))?;
    fs::write(
        output.join("comparison.json"),
        serde_json::to_vec_pretty(&comparison.snapshot())?,
    )?;
    if !comparison.policy().allows_publication() {
        return Err("Comparison policy blocked publication; inspect comparison.json".into());
    }
    let prepared = next.prepare_publication(BuildOptions::to(&candidate).update_from(&baseline))?;
    let review = prepared
        .report()
        .comparison()
        .ok_or("Missing update comparison")?;
    fs::write(
        output.join("review.json"),
        serde_json::to_vec_pretty(&review.snapshot())?,
    )?;
    if !review.policy().allows_publication() {
        return Err("Prepared candidate blocked; inspect review.json".into());
    }
    let result = prepared.publish()?;
    println!("{}", result.artifact().path().display());
    Ok(())
}
```

```sh
cargo run -- recipe output/rust
```

## Python

Ordinary CPython 3.11+ with a platform wheel; 3.11–3.14 is covered by release checks. On Windows, activate with `.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1`. Use public Anki Forge 0.3.1.

```sh
mkdir json-deck
cd json-deck
python -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install ankiforge==0.3.1
```

Save as `main.py` (create `recipe/` alongside `main.py`):

```python
"""Generate and review an answer-only update from caller-parsed JSON."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
import sys
from ankiforge import BuildOptions, CompareOptions, Content, Media, Note, Project


def project(source: Path, version: str) -> Project:
    data = json.loads((source / version).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    image = Media.file(source / 'cell.png')
    audio = Media.file(source / 'tone.wav')
    result = Project(data['namespace'], default_deck=data['deck'])
    for row in data['notes']:
        front = Content.sequence([row['front'], image.image(), audio.sound()])
        result.add(row['id'], Note.basic(front, row['back']))
    return result


source = Path(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 'recipe')
output = Path(sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else 'output/python')
output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
baseline, candidate = output / 'v1.apkg', output / 'v2.apkg'
if baseline.exists() or candidate.exists():
    raise RuntimeError('Choose a fresh output directory; keep original releases')
project(source, 'v1.json').build(BuildOptions.to(baseline))
next_project = project(source, 'v2.json')
comparison = next_project.compare(CompareOptions.against(baseline))
(output / 'comparison.json').write_text(json.dumps(comparison.snapshot(), indent=2), encoding='utf-8')
if not comparison.allows_publication:
    raise RuntimeError('Comparison policy blocked publication; inspect comparison.json')
prepared = next_project.prepare_publication(BuildOptions.to(candidate).update_from(baseline))
try:
    review = prepared.report.comparison
    if review is None:
        raise RuntimeError('Missing update comparison')
    (output / 'review.json').write_text(json.dumps(review.snapshot(), indent=2), encoding='utf-8')
    if not review.allows_publication:
        raise RuntimeError('Prepared candidate blocked; inspect review.json')
    result = prepared.publish()
    print(result.artifact.path)
finally:
    prepared.close()
```

```sh
python main.py recipe output/python
```

## Node

Node.js 22.13+ and a matching native optional dependency. This program compiles TypeScript to JavaScript and runs on Node.js. Use public Anki Forge 0.3.1.

```sh
mkdir json-deck
cd json-deck
npm init -y
npm install --include=optional ankiforge@0.3.1
npm install --save-dev typescript@6.0.3 @types/node@24.13.6
```

Save as `main.mts` (create `recipe/` alongside `main.mts`):

```typescript
import { readFile, mkdir, access, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import path from 'node:path';
import { Project, Note, Content, Media, BuildOptions, CompareOptions } from 'ankiforge';

interface Dataset {
  namespace: string;
  deck: string;
  notes: { id: string; front: string; back: string }[];
}

async function project(source: string, version: string): Promise<Project> {
  const data: Dataset = JSON.parse(await readFile(path.join(source, version), 'utf8'));
  const image = await Media.file(path.join(source, 'cell.png'));
  const audio = await Media.file(path.join(source, 'tone.wav'));
  const result = new Project(data.namespace).defaultDeck(data.deck);
  for (const row of data.notes) {
    const front = Content.sequence([row.front, image.image(), audio.sound()]);
    result.add(row.id, Note.basic(front, row.back));
  }
  return result;
}

const source = process.argv[2] ?? 'recipe';
const output = process.argv[3] ?? 'output/node';
await mkdir(output, { recursive: true });
const baseline = path.join(output, 'v1.apkg');
const candidate = path.join(output, 'v2.apkg');
for (const file of [baseline, candidate]) {
  const exists = await access(file).then(() => true, error => {
    if (error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;
    throw error;
  });
  if (exists) throw new Error('Choose a fresh output directory; keep original releases');
}
const first = await (await project(source, 'v1.json')).build(BuildOptions.to(baseline));
await first.artifact.close();
const next = await project(source, 'v2.json');
const comparison = await next.compare(CompareOptions.against(baseline));
await writeFile(path.join(output, 'comparison.json'), JSON.stringify(comparison.snapshot(), null, 2));
if (!comparison.policy.allows_publication) {
  throw new Error('Comparison policy blocked publication; inspect comparison.json');
}
const prepared = await next.preparePublication(BuildOptions.to(candidate).updateFrom(baseline));
try {
  const review = prepared.report.comparison;
  if (!review) throw new Error('Missing update comparison');
  await writeFile(path.join(output, 'review.json'), JSON.stringify(review.snapshot(), null, 2));
  if (!review.policy.allows_publication) throw new Error('Prepared candidate blocked; inspect review.json');
  const result = await prepared.publish();
  console.log(result.artifact.path);
  await result.artifact.close();
} finally {
  await prepared.close();
}
```

```sh
npx tsc main.mts --target ES2022 --module NodeNext --moduleResolution NodeNext --strict --outDir dist --types node
node dist/main.mjs recipe output/node
```

## Check and import the result

The selected program prints `output/<language>/v2.apkg`. Keep `v1.apkg` alongside it; `comparison.json` and `review.json` record `RISK.NOTE_CHANGED`, no added or removed notes, and `policy.allows_publication: true` for this answer-only edit. The program checks the policy again on the prepared candidate before publishing. It refuses to reuse an output directory containing either release.

Import `v1.apkg` into Anki: expect the Biology deck with three Basic cards, the cell image and the tone. Then import `v2.apkg`: check that the first answer becomes “The basic structural and functional unit of life”, with three notes remaining. The namespace `biology-json` identifies this publishing project. Each business ID is a stable note key; Anki Forge derives the GUID used by Anki from that identity. Keep the namespace and those three keys unchanged.

Use the **original distribution** v1 APKG as the update baseline, never an Anki re-export. Client import matching, local edits and scheduling depend on Anki version, note types and import settings; validate your target client before a release. Importing a package does not remove notes omitted from a later package. A successful compare/build is not a guarantee about every learner’s review state.

See [update conditions](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/updates/), [media](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/media/), [API navigation](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/api/) and [library selection](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/anki-forge-vs-genanki/).

# Update Anki decks with stable note IDs

Canonical page: https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/updates/
Language: en
Description: Release a new version of a generated Anki deck: keep stable note IDs, build from the previous original APKG and review the comparison before publishing.

Publish corrections or new cards for an Anki deck you have already distributed. Stable note IDs help Anki Forge and Anki recognize existing notes instead of treating them as new ones; Anki’s import settings and newer local edits still affect what changes.

Keep the project namespace and note/model/field/template keys stable. Build each new release from the previous **original distribution APKG**, which carries complete versioned identity evidence. Save that package with its source revision.

## Run two versions and compare

```sh
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example docs_workflow -- target/docs-examples
```

This writes `spanish-v1.apkg` and `spanish-v2.apkg`, compares the changed answer, and checks the updated package counts. The executable source is:

```rust
fn vocabulary(answer: &str) -> anyhow::Result<Project> {
    let mut project = Project::new("docs-spanish-updates")?.default_deck("Spanish");
    project.add("hola", Note::basic("hola", answer))?;
    Ok(project)
}

fn updates(output: &Path) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let previous = output.join("spanish-v1.apkg");
    let next = output.join("spanish-v2.apkg");
    vocabulary("hello")?.build(BuildOptions::to(&previous))?;
    let project = vocabulary("hello; hi")?;
    let comparison = project.compare(CompareOptions::against(&previous))?;
    ensure!(comparison.policy().allows_publication());
    let built = project.build(BuildOptions::to(&next).update_from(&previous))?;
    verify(&built, 1, 1, 0)?;
    ensure!(built.report().comparison().is_some());
    Ok(())
}
```

`compare` completes successfully even when findings would block publication. Read `comparison.policy().allows_publication()` separately from the original risk level and evidence. `build(...update_from(...))` runs the same analysis and returns `BuildError` if its policy blocks the candidate, before publication.

## Policy and inspection limits

This full program selects a stricter threshold and uses the same configuration for comparison and update:

```rust
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Note, Project};
use ankiforge::build::InspectLimits;
use ankiforge::update::{CompareOptions, RiskLevel, UpdatePolicy};

fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let mut first = Project::new("policy-example")?;
    first.add("cell", Note::basic("Cell?", "Unit of life"))?;
    first.build(BuildOptions::to("policy-v1.apkg"))?;
    let mut next = Project::new("policy-example")?;
    next.add("cell", Note::basic("Cell?", "The basic unit of life"))?;
    let mut limits = InspectLimits::default();
    limits.max_collection_bytes = 1 << 30;
    let policy = UpdatePolicy::default().fail_on(RiskLevel::Medium);
    let comparison = next.compare(CompareOptions::against("policy-v1.apkg")
        .inspect_limits(limits.clone()).update_policy(policy.clone()))?;
    assert!(comparison.policy().allows_publication());
    next.build(BuildOptions::to("policy-v2.apkg").update_from("policy-v1.apkg")
        .inspect_limits(limits).update_policy(policy))?;
    Ok(())
}
```

The default policy blocks High and Critical findings. After reviewing a specific category, a caller can deliberately choose `UpdatePolicy::default().allow(RiskCode::NoteRemoved)`. It accepts **all findings in that category**, retaining their original level and evidence. It does not claim to approve selected notes individually. An allowance with no matching finding produces a warning; unknown risk codes are rejected. Do not automatically allow every code returned by a comparison.

Missing or corrupt evidence, namespace mismatch, invalid candidate data and inspection limits are hard errors, not allowable risk categories. Comparison returns an error with completed observations when analysis cannot finish. Explicit policy on a create request without `update_from` is a configuration error regardless of setter order.

## Evidence and identity

The package includes `ankiforge-identity.json` with the `ankiforge-identity-v1` format. It binds model/config IDs, note GUIDs, historical field/template slots, card/mask ordinals, revisions and media to the actual collection and payloads. Anki re-export does not preserve this evidence and is not a usable update baseline. Missing evidence is never silently reconstructed.

Display-name and content edits preserve identity keys. Unchanged content keeps its baseline revision; changed content advances it. Reordering fields/templates preserves historical mappings. Retired identities remain reserved so that restoring the same key can reuse them. A note key cannot move to another model, and a model key cannot change between normal and Cloze kinds.

## Client import behavior and release review

An APKG is a distribution package, not deletion synchronization. Omitting notes, fields, templates or masks does not delete existing learner data. Field/template schema changes and sort-field changes are high-risk because Anki merge and import settings affect their behavior. Schema changes can copy models or update target note timestamps before note-content comparison.

Test first import and updates into an existing collection on the clients you support. Check fields, GUIDs, card sets, local edits and existing scheduling with the intended merge and note-update settings. Stable identity alone does not promise that newer local edits are overwritten or deleted history is restored.

Write candidates to a path separate from the archived baseline. After review, distribute the accepted package and retain it as the next release’s evidence. See [build guarantees](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/build-guarantees/) for ownership and publication facts.

## Build once, review then publish

This API is included in the public `0.3.1` package.

Build once, inspect the report, then publish the same candidate file. Reviewing and then running a second ordinary build creates another candidate; prepared publication keeps the actual APKG tied to the reviewed report.

```rust
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Note, Project};

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let mut project = Project::new("spanish")?.default_deck("Spanish");
    project.add("es:hola", Note::basic("hola", "hello"))?;
    project.build(BuildOptions::to("spanish-original.apkg"))?;

    let mut next = Project::new("spanish")?.default_deck("Spanish");
    next.add("es:hola", Note::basic("hola", "hello; hi"))?;
    let prepared = next.prepare_publication(
        BuildOptions::to("spanish-reviewed.apkg").update_from("spanish-original.apkg"),
    )?;
    println!("{:?}", prepared.report().comparison());
    if prepared
        .report()
        .comparison()
        .is_some_and(|report| report.policy().allows_publication())
    {
        let output = prepared.publish()?;
        println!("{}", output.artifact().path().display());
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

From the pinned source checkout, save the complete program above as `anki_forge/examples/docs_publication.rs` (this guide adds the example; it is not bundled in `1199196`). Then run:

```sh
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example docs_publication
```

The example writes `spanish-original.apkg` and, when the policy allows publication, `spanish-reviewed.apkg` to the repository root. Preparation does not publish the destination. Review the findings and test your client import before approving distribution; the example automatically publishes only this simple content edit when its policy allows it. The benchmark does not measure this workflow.

See [build lifecycle](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/build-guarantees/#prepared-publication-from-source), [Rust API](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/rust-api/#review-once-publish-once), [Node API](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/node-api/#prepare-review-and-publish) and [Python API](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/python-api/#prepare-review-and-publish).

# Add images and audio to Anki cards

Canonical page: https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/media/
Language: en
Description: Add images and audio to generated Anki cards with Rust, Python or Node.js. Import files, compose card content, and manage export names, MIME types and budgets.

Package images and audio into generated Anki cards, such as vocabulary cards with pronunciation audio or diagram questions. Anki Forge copies the files you provide into the APKG; creating the audio or images, for example with text-to-speech, requires a separate tool. The examples use Rust; batch import below also shows the Python and Node.js calls.

A `Media` value owns an immutable snapshot. Import files with `Media::file` or native bytes with an explicit MIME type via `Media::bytes`. After successful import, modifying or deleting the source file cannot change the asset. Clones share storage and can be used across projects.

## Execute the media workflow

From the repository root:

```sh
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example docs_workflow -- target/docs-examples
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example target_api_media
```

The workflow uses repository PNG/WAV fixtures and writes `media.apkg` with one note, one card and three assets. The second example generates its own tiny image and audio, includes CSS-linked and explicit media, and writes `spanish-media.apkg`.

```rust
fn media(output: &Path, image: &Path, sound: &Path) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let image = Media::file(image)?.with_export_name("cell.png")?;
    let sound = Media::file(sound)?;
    let mut project = Project::new("docs-media")?;
    project.add("cell", Note::basic(image.image(), sound.sound()))?;
    let css = Media::bytes(b".card { color: navy; }".to_vec(), "text/css")?
        .with_export_name("course.css")?;
    project.add_asset(css)?;
    let built = project.build(BuildOptions::to(output.join("media.apkg")))?;
    verify(&built, 1, 1, 3)?;
    Ok(())
}
```

## Compose content and explicit assets

This complete program uses `fixtures/pixel.png`, `fixtures/silence.wav`, and `fixtures/labels.woff`. In your application, pass your own source paths. The fixture font is the repository’s redistributable test font.

```rust
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Content, Field, Media, NoteType, Project, Template};

fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let image = Media::file("fixtures/pixel.png")?.with_export_name("badge.png")?;
    let sound = Media::file("fixtures/silence.wav")?;
    let font = Media::file("fixtures/labels.woff")?.with_export_name("labels.woff")?;
    let model = NoteType::builder("media-card")
        .field(Field::new("front"))
        .field(Field::new("back"))
        .template(Template::new("card")
            .front(r#"{{front}}<img src="badge.png">"#)
            .back("{{FrontSide}}<hr>{{back}}"))
        .css("@font-face { font-family: labels; src: url('labels.woff'); } .card { font-family: labels; }")
        .asset(font)
        .asset(image.clone())
        .build()?;
    let mut project = Project::new("media-guide")?;
    project.add("cell", model.note()
        .field("front", Content::sequence([Content::text("Cell "), image.image()]))
        .field("back", sound.sound()))?;
    let output = project.build(BuildOptions::to("media-guide.apkg"))?;
    assert_eq!(output.report().counts().media, 3);
    Ok(())
}
```

Typed `image()` and `sound()` values retain dependencies until export. Manual HTML/CSS/script references need `builder.asset(media)` or `project.add_asset(media)`; the library does not infer file contents from arbitrary strings. An explicit asset is included even without a statically detectable reference.

Pass the literal filename to `with_export_name`. Typed sound references escape HTML entities when rendered, so a name such as `tone&copy;.mp3` still refers to that exact asset. Do not pre-escape the filename. Percent signs and fragment characters in sound filenames remain literal; they are not URL paths.

## Names, MIME and budgets

Default export names are content-derived and independent of the source path. Use `with_export_name` before creating references when a fixed filename is needed. Renaming a clone does not rename earlier clones or content nodes.

Names cannot contain paths, controls or nonportable reserved names. Conflict checks use Unicode NFC plus case folding: case-only or normalization-only variants also conflict. Exactly identical name/content pairs are idempotent; different contents under one name fail without partial registration.

The complete export filename, including its extension, is limited to 255 UTF-8 bytes. Project and template-bundle JSON Schemas check filename syntax and character count; the loaders additionally check this byte budget. For example, 128 repetitions of `é` pass the schema’s character limit but occupy 256 bytes and return `MEDIA.EXPORT_NAME_INVALID` when loaded. Use `tools::load_project` or `NoteType::from_bundle` to validate the complete input before building.

MIME syntax and identifiable content must agree. Native bytes have no 64 KiB inline restriction. The default import budget is 256 MiB per asset; `file_with_limits` and `bytes_with_limits` accept `MediaLimits { max_bytes }` before reading. Large snapshots may spill to temporary storage, cleaned up when the last owner disappears. Snapshot ownership does not promise an atomic filesystem view of a source being modified concurrently during import.

Project JSON applies the same default per-asset budget while decoding an inline `bytes` array. It stops at the first excess byte without collecting the rest of the array, and retains a `MediaError` with the limit and observed byte count. The count at rejection is a lower bound; it is not the unread array’s total size.

A valid media package does not prove codec playback on every Anki client. Test images, sound and fonts on your target clients. See [troubleshooting](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/docs/troubleshooting/#media-and-templates).

### Typed image and sound usage

Constructors stay infallible. `Project::add` checks the retained import MIME: images require `image/*`, sound references accept `audio/*` and `video/*`. `application/octet-stream`, text, fonts and PDF fail typed usage with `NOTE.MEDIA_USAGE_INVALID`; register them as explicit assets for raw HTML/CSS. Valid explicit unknown image/video MIME declarations pass category validation, without certifying that a decoder or player supports the bytes. Renaming a file never changes retained MIME. Build still sniffs staged bytes and validates the export extension independently: PNG named `wrong.mp3` can pass image addition and fail build with `MEDIA.DECLARED_MIME_MISMATCH`.

## Batch media import

These methods are included in the public `0.3.1` package.

Import a collection with bounded concurrency, keep input order, and retain owned media snapshots for later export:

```rust
use ankiforge::Media;
let images = Media::files(["first.png", "second.png"])?;
```

Node uses `await Media.files(['first.png', 'second.png'])`; Python uses `Media.files(['first.png', 'second.png'])`.

### Batch behavior and budgets

Use `Media::files(paths)` in Rust, `await Media.files(paths)` in Node, or `Media.files(paths)` in Python to import files in input order with at most four workers per call. Batches below 16 files run serially. Rust also provides `files_with_limits`; Node and Python accept the same limits as `file`. The limit applies to each asset. If an import fails, the call waits for started work, drops the batch’s snapshots, and returns the first error in input order. Existing media owners remain valid. Python releases the GIL during import; Node performs the work off the event loop. Single-file imports remain immediate owned snapshots; callers must opt into the batch method for import concurrency.

Live snapshots share a **64 MiB** process-wide memory budget. Individual assets larger than 1 MiB still stream to temporary files. Encoded media share a lazily allocated **16 MiB** buffer pool per preparation and spill when it fills. These budgets exclude other working memory and are not an RSS cap; concurrent builds can each own an encoding pool.

# 用 JSON 数据生成并更新 Anki 牌组

Canonical page: https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/json-to-anki/
Language: zh-CN
Description: 用 Rust、Node 或 Python 读取 JSON，打包图片和音频，再检查仅修改答案的更新。

从 JSON 读取三个生物学问题，添加共享图片与音频，导出原始 APKG 和经过检查的仅修改答案的更新。每个版本应包含 **3 条笔记、3 张卡片和 2 个媒体文件**。选择下方任一 SDK，每份都是完整程序。普通导出不需要安装 Anki。

由 Anki Forge 维护者维护 · 2026-10-25 复核。

## 共享输入

下载 [v1.json](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/v1.json)、[v2.json](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/v2.json)、[cell.png](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/cell.png) 和 [tone.wav](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/tone.wav)。图片是细胞示意图；音频是短合成音，并非词汇朗读。在每个新应用目录中，将这四个文件放入 `recipe/`：

```text
json-deck/
  recipe/
    v1.json
    v2.json
    cell.png
    tone.wav
```

两份 JSON 都包含 `namespace`、`deck` 和三条 `notes`，每条有持久 `id`、`front` 与 `back`。v2 只改变第一个答案。JSON 由调用方解析；Anki Forge 负责内容编写和 APKG 生成。对于不可信输入，创建笔记前应校验应用自己的 schema。

## Rust

Rust 1.92+。JSON 解析使用 `serde` 与 `serde_json`。使用公开 Anki Forge 0.3.1。

```sh
cargo new json-deck
cd json-deck
cargo add ankiforge@0.3.1
cargo add serde --features derive
cargo add serde_json
```

保存为 `src/main.rs`（在 `Cargo.toml` 同级创建 `recipe/`）：

```rust
use ankiforge::update::CompareOptions;
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Content, Media, Note, Project};
use serde::Deserialize;
use std::{fs, path::Path};

#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct Dataset {
    namespace: String,
    deck: String,
    notes: Vec<Row>,
}

#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct Row {
    id: String,
    front: String,
    back: String,
}

fn project(input: &Path, version: &str) -> Result<Project, Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let data: Dataset = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(input.join(version))?)?;
    let image = Media::file(input.join("cell.png"))?;
    let audio = Media::file(input.join("tone.wav"))?;
    let mut project = Project::new(data.namespace)?.default_deck(data.deck);
    for row in data.notes {
        let front = Content::sequence([Content::text(row.front), image.image(), audio.sound()]);
        project.add(row.id, Note::basic(front, row.back))?;
    }
    Ok(project)
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let args: Vec<_> = std::env::args().collect();
    let input = Path::new(args.get(1).map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("recipe"));
    let output = Path::new(args.get(2).map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("output/rust"));
    fs::create_dir_all(output)?;
    let baseline = output.join("v1.apkg");
    let candidate = output.join("v2.apkg");
    if baseline.exists() || candidate.exists() {
        return Err("Choose a fresh output directory; keep original releases".into());
    }
    project(input, "v1.json")?.build(BuildOptions::to(&baseline))?;
    let next = project(input, "v2.json")?;
    let comparison = next.compare(CompareOptions::against(&baseline))?;
    fs::write(
        output.join("comparison.json"),
        serde_json::to_vec_pretty(&comparison.snapshot())?,
    )?;
    if !comparison.policy().allows_publication() {
        return Err("Comparison policy blocked publication; inspect comparison.json".into());
    }
    let prepared = next.prepare_publication(BuildOptions::to(&candidate).update_from(&baseline))?;
    let review = prepared
        .report()
        .comparison()
        .ok_or("Missing update comparison")?;
    fs::write(
        output.join("review.json"),
        serde_json::to_vec_pretty(&review.snapshot())?,
    )?;
    if !review.policy().allows_publication() {
        return Err("Prepared candidate blocked; inspect review.json".into());
    }
    let result = prepared.publish()?;
    println!("{}", result.artifact().path().display());
    Ok(())
}
```

```sh
cargo run -- recipe output/rust
```

## Python

普通 CPython 3.11+ 及匹配平台 wheel；发布检查覆盖 3.11–3.14。Windows 使用 `.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1` 激活。使用公开 Anki Forge 0.3.1。

```sh
mkdir json-deck
cd json-deck
python -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install ankiforge==0.3.1
```

保存为 `main.py`（在 `main.py` 同级创建 `recipe/`）：

```python
"""Generate and review an answer-only update from caller-parsed JSON."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
import sys
from ankiforge import BuildOptions, CompareOptions, Content, Media, Note, Project


def project(source: Path, version: str) -> Project:
    data = json.loads((source / version).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    image = Media.file(source / 'cell.png')
    audio = Media.file(source / 'tone.wav')
    result = Project(data['namespace'], default_deck=data['deck'])
    for row in data['notes']:
        front = Content.sequence([row['front'], image.image(), audio.sound()])
        result.add(row['id'], Note.basic(front, row['back']))
    return result


source = Path(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 'recipe')
output = Path(sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else 'output/python')
output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
baseline, candidate = output / 'v1.apkg', output / 'v2.apkg'
if baseline.exists() or candidate.exists():
    raise RuntimeError('Choose a fresh output directory; keep original releases')
project(source, 'v1.json').build(BuildOptions.to(baseline))
next_project = project(source, 'v2.json')
comparison = next_project.compare(CompareOptions.against(baseline))
(output / 'comparison.json').write_text(json.dumps(comparison.snapshot(), indent=2), encoding='utf-8')
if not comparison.allows_publication:
    raise RuntimeError('Comparison policy blocked publication; inspect comparison.json')
prepared = next_project.prepare_publication(BuildOptions.to(candidate).update_from(baseline))
try:
    review = prepared.report.comparison
    if review is None:
        raise RuntimeError('Missing update comparison')
    (output / 'review.json').write_text(json.dumps(review.snapshot(), indent=2), encoding='utf-8')
    if not review.allows_publication:
        raise RuntimeError('Prepared candidate blocked; inspect review.json')
    result = prepared.publish()
    print(result.artifact.path)
finally:
    prepared.close()
```

```sh
python main.py recipe output/python
```

## Node

Node.js 22.13+ 及匹配原生可选依赖。程序将 TypeScript 编译为 JavaScript，再在 Node.js 上运行。使用公开 Anki Forge 0.3.1。

```sh
mkdir json-deck
cd json-deck
npm init -y
npm install --include=optional ankiforge@0.3.1
npm install --save-dev typescript@6.0.3 @types/node@24.13.6
```

保存为 `main.mts`（在 `main.mts` 同级创建 `recipe/`）：

```typescript
import { readFile, mkdir, access, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import path from 'node:path';
import { Project, Note, Content, Media, BuildOptions, CompareOptions } from 'ankiforge';

interface Dataset {
  namespace: string;
  deck: string;
  notes: { id: string; front: string; back: string }[];
}

async function project(source: string, version: string): Promise<Project> {
  const data: Dataset = JSON.parse(await readFile(path.join(source, version), 'utf8'));
  const image = await Media.file(path.join(source, 'cell.png'));
  const audio = await Media.file(path.join(source, 'tone.wav'));
  const result = new Project(data.namespace).defaultDeck(data.deck);
  for (const row of data.notes) {
    const front = Content.sequence([row.front, image.image(), audio.sound()]);
    result.add(row.id, Note.basic(front, row.back));
  }
  return result;
}

const source = process.argv[2] ?? 'recipe';
const output = process.argv[3] ?? 'output/node';
await mkdir(output, { recursive: true });
const baseline = path.join(output, 'v1.apkg');
const candidate = path.join(output, 'v2.apkg');
for (const file of [baseline, candidate]) {
  const exists = await access(file).then(() => true, error => {
    if (error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;
    throw error;
  });
  if (exists) throw new Error('Choose a fresh output directory; keep original releases');
}
const first = await (await project(source, 'v1.json')).build(BuildOptions.to(baseline));
await first.artifact.close();
const next = await project(source, 'v2.json');
const comparison = await next.compare(CompareOptions.against(baseline));
await writeFile(path.join(output, 'comparison.json'), JSON.stringify(comparison.snapshot(), null, 2));
if (!comparison.policy.allows_publication) {
  throw new Error('Comparison policy blocked publication; inspect comparison.json');
}
const prepared = await next.preparePublication(BuildOptions.to(candidate).updateFrom(baseline));
try {
  const review = prepared.report.comparison;
  if (!review) throw new Error('Missing update comparison');
  await writeFile(path.join(output, 'review.json'), JSON.stringify(review.snapshot(), null, 2));
  if (!review.policy.allows_publication) throw new Error('Prepared candidate blocked; inspect review.json');
  const result = await prepared.publish();
  console.log(result.artifact.path);
  await result.artifact.close();
} finally {
  await prepared.close();
}
```

```sh
npx tsc main.mts --target ES2022 --module NodeNext --moduleResolution NodeNext --strict --outDir dist --types node
node dist/main.mjs recipe output/node
```

## 检查并导入结果

所选程序输出 `output/<language>/v2.apkg`。将 `v1.apkg` 保留在旁边；`comparison.json` 和 `review.json` 记录 `RISK.NOTE_CHANGED`，没有新增或移除笔记，且对这次仅修改答案的编辑给出 `policy.allows_publication: true`。发布前，程序在预备候选包上再次检查策略。它拒绝复用已包含任一版本的输出目录。

将 `v1.apkg` 导入 Anki，应看到 Biology 牌组的三张 Basic 卡片、细胞图片与合成音。再导入 `v2.apkg`，检查第一个答案变成“The basic structural and functional unit of life”，且仍有三条笔记。命名空间 `biology-json` 标识该发布项目。每个业务 ID 是稳定笔记键；Anki Forge 根据该身份派生 Anki 使用的 GUID。保持命名空间和这三个键不变。

更新基线必须是**原始分发** v1 APKG，不能使用 Anki 重新导出的文件。客户端导入匹配、本地编辑和调度取决于 Anki 版本、笔记类型与导入设置；发布前验证目标客户端。导入包不会删除后续包中省略的笔记。比较或构建成功不保证每位学习者的复习状态。

参见[更新条件](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/updates/)、[媒体](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/media/)、[API 导航](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/api/)和[选库指南](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/anki-forge-vs-genanki/)。

# 用稳定笔记 ID 更新 Anki 牌组

Canonical page: https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/updates/
Language: zh-CN
Description: 发布生成牌组的新版本：保持稳定笔记 ID，以上一版原始 APKG 为基线构建，并在分发前检查比较结果。

为已经分发的 Anki 牌组发布修正或新增卡片。稳定笔记 ID 帮助 Anki Forge 和 Anki 识别已有笔记，而不是把它们当成新笔记；Anki 导入设置与较新的本地编辑仍会影响最终变化。

保持项目命名空间和笔记、模型、字段、模板键稳定。每次新版本基于之前的**原始分发 APKG** 构建，该包携带完整、带版本的身份证据。将包和源代码修订一起保存。

## 运行两个版本并比较

```sh
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example docs_workflow -- target/docs-examples
```

这会写出 `spanish-v1.apkg` 和 `spanish-v2.apkg`，比较修改后的答案，并检查更新包的数量。可执行源码如下：

```rust
fn vocabulary(answer: &str) -> anyhow::Result<Project> {
    let mut project = Project::new("docs-spanish-updates")?.default_deck("Spanish");
    project.add("hola", Note::basic("hola", answer))?;
    Ok(project)
}

fn updates(output: &Path) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let previous = output.join("spanish-v1.apkg");
    let next = output.join("spanish-v2.apkg");
    vocabulary("hello")?.build(BuildOptions::to(&previous))?;
    let project = vocabulary("hello; hi")?;
    let comparison = project.compare(CompareOptions::against(&previous))?;
    ensure!(comparison.policy().allows_publication());
    let built = project.build(BuildOptions::to(&next).update_from(&previous))?;
    verify(&built, 1, 1, 0)?;
    ensure!(built.report().comparison().is_some());
    Ok(())
}
```

即使发现项会阻止发布，`compare` 也可以成功完成。请分别读取 `comparison.policy().allows_publication()`、原始风险级别和证据。`build(...update_from(...))` 执行相同分析；若策略阻止候选包，则在发布前返回 `BuildError`。

## 策略与检查限制

这份完整程序选择更严格的阈值，并对比较和更新使用相同配置：

```rust
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Note, Project};
use ankiforge::build::InspectLimits;
use ankiforge::update::{CompareOptions, RiskLevel, UpdatePolicy};

fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let mut first = Project::new("policy-example")?;
    first.add("cell", Note::basic("Cell?", "Unit of life"))?;
    first.build(BuildOptions::to("policy-v1.apkg"))?;
    let mut next = Project::new("policy-example")?;
    next.add("cell", Note::basic("Cell?", "The basic unit of life"))?;
    let mut limits = InspectLimits::default();
    limits.max_collection_bytes = 1 << 30;
    let policy = UpdatePolicy::default().fail_on(RiskLevel::Medium);
    let comparison = next.compare(CompareOptions::against("policy-v1.apkg")
        .inspect_limits(limits.clone()).update_policy(policy.clone()))?;
    assert!(comparison.policy().allows_publication());
    next.build(BuildOptions::to("policy-v2.apkg").update_from("policy-v1.apkg")
        .inspect_limits(limits).update_policy(policy))?;
    Ok(())
}
```

默认策略阻止 High 和 Critical 发现项。审阅特定类别后，调用方可有意选择 `UpdatePolicy::default().allow(RiskCode::NoteRemoved)`。它放行**该类别中的所有发现项**，同时保留原级别和证据；并不表示逐条批准指定笔记。没有匹配发现项的放行会产生警告；未知风险码被拒绝。不要自动放行比较返回的每一个码。

缺失或损坏的证据、命名空间不匹配、无效候选数据和检查限制都是硬错误，不是可放行的风险类别。分析无法完成时，比较返回错误及已完成的观察结果。对没有 `update_from` 的新建请求显式设置策略属于配置错误，与 setter 调用顺序无关。

## 证据与身份

包内包含 `ankiforge-identity.json`，格式为 `ankiforge-identity-v1`。它将模型或配置 ID、笔记 GUID、历史字段或模板槽位、卡片或遮罩序号、修订和媒体绑定到实际集合与载荷。Anki 重新导出不保留该证据，不能作为更新基线。缺失证据绝不会被静默重建。

显示名称和内容编辑保留身份键。内容未变时保留基线修订；内容改变时推进修订。字段或模板重排保留历史映射。退役身份继续保留，恢复相同键时可复用。笔记键不能移到另一模型，模型键也不能在普通与 Cloze 类型间改变。

## 客户端导入行为与发布检查

APKG 是分发包，不是删除同步。省略笔记、字段、模板或遮罩，不会删除学习者已有数据。字段或模板 schema 和排序字段变化属于高风险，因为 Anki 合并与导入设置会影响行为。Schema 变化可能复制模型，或在笔记内容比较前更新目标笔记的时间戳。

在支持的客户端测试首次导入以及导入已有集合的更新。使用目标合并与笔记更新设置，检查字段、GUID、卡片集合、本地编辑和已有调度。仅稳定身份不保证较新本地编辑被覆盖，也不保证已删除的历史被恢复。

将候选包写到与归档基线不同的路径。审阅后分发被接受的包，并将它保留为下一次发布的证据。所有权和发布事实见[构建保证](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/build-guarantees/)。

## 构建一次，审阅后发布

此 API 已包含在公开 `0.3.1` 包中。

构建一次，检查报告，然后发布同一个候选文件。审阅后再运行一次普通构建会创建另一个候选包；预备发布使实际 APKG 始终与已审阅报告对应。

```rust
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Note, Project};

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let mut project = Project::new("spanish")?.default_deck("Spanish");
    project.add("es:hola", Note::basic("hola", "hello"))?;
    project.build(BuildOptions::to("spanish-original.apkg"))?;

    let mut next = Project::new("spanish")?.default_deck("Spanish");
    next.add("es:hola", Note::basic("hola", "hello; hi"))?;
    let prepared = next.prepare_publication(
        BuildOptions::to("spanish-reviewed.apkg").update_from("spanish-original.apkg"),
    )?;
    println!("{:?}", prepared.report().comparison());
    if prepared
        .report()
        .comparison()
        .is_some_and(|report| report.policy().allows_publication())
    {
        let output = prepared.publish()?;
        println!("{}", output.artifact().path().display());
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

在固定修订的源码目录中，把上面的完整程序保存为 `anki_forge/examples/docs_publication.rs`（本指南新增该示例；`1199196` 中未包含它），然后运行：

```sh
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example docs_publication
```

示例在仓库根目录写出 `spanish-original.apkg`，并在策略允许发布时写出 `spanish-reviewed.apkg`。预备阶段不发布到目标。批准分发前，应审阅发现项并测试客户端导入；此示例只在策略允许时自动发布这次简单内容编辑。基准测试未测量该流程。

参见[构建生命周期](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/build-guarantees/#prepared-publication-from-source)、[Rust API](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/rust-api/#review-once-publish-once)、[Node API](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/node-api/#prepare-review-and-publish)和 [Python API](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/python-api/#prepare-review-and-publish)。

# 为 Anki 卡片添加图片与音频

Canonical page: https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/media/
Language: zh-CN
Description: 用 Rust、Python 或 Node.js 为生成的 Anki 卡片添加图片和音频：导入文件、组合卡片内容，并管理导出名称、MIME 类型与媒体预算。

把图片和音频打包进生成的 Anki 卡片，例如带发音音频的单词卡或示意图题目。Anki Forge 将你提供的文件复制进 APKG；生成音频或图片（例如语音合成）需要使用其他工具。示例使用 Rust；下文的批量导入也给出了 Python 和 Node.js 调用。

`Media` 值拥有不可变快照。使用 `Media::file` 导入文件，或通过带显式 MIME 类型的 `Media::bytes` 导入原生字节。成功导入后，修改或删除源文件都不会改变该资源。克隆共享存储，可跨项目使用。

## 运行媒体流程

在仓库根目录运行：

```sh
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example docs_workflow -- target/docs-examples
cargo run --locked -p ankiforge --example target_api_media
```

该流程使用仓库 PNG/WAV 测试素材，写出包含一条笔记、一张卡片和三个资源的 `media.apkg`。第二个示例自行生成小图像和音频，包含 CSS 引用及显式声明的媒体，并写出 `spanish-media.apkg`。

```rust
fn media(output: &Path, image: &Path, sound: &Path) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let image = Media::file(image)?.with_export_name("cell.png")?;
    let sound = Media::file(sound)?;
    let mut project = Project::new("docs-media")?;
    project.add("cell", Note::basic(image.image(), sound.sound()))?;
    let css = Media::bytes(b".card { color: navy; }".to_vec(), "text/css")?
        .with_export_name("course.css")?;
    project.add_asset(css)?;
    let built = project.build(BuildOptions::to(output.join("media.apkg")))?;
    verify(&built, 1, 1, 3)?;
    Ok(())
}
```

## 组合内容与显式资源

这份完整程序使用 `fixtures/pixel.png`、`fixtures/silence.wav` 和 `fixtures/labels.woff`。在应用中请传入自己的源路径。测试字体是仓库中允许再分发的测试用字体。

```rust
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Content, Field, Media, NoteType, Project, Template};

fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let image = Media::file("fixtures/pixel.png")?.with_export_name("badge.png")?;
    let sound = Media::file("fixtures/silence.wav")?;
    let font = Media::file("fixtures/labels.woff")?.with_export_name("labels.woff")?;
    let model = NoteType::builder("media-card")
        .field(Field::new("front"))
        .field(Field::new("back"))
        .template(Template::new("card")
            .front(r#"{{front}}<img src="badge.png">"#)
            .back("{{FrontSide}}<hr>{{back}}"))
        .css("@font-face { font-family: labels; src: url('labels.woff'); } .card { font-family: labels; }")
        .asset(font)
        .asset(image.clone())
        .build()?;
    let mut project = Project::new("media-guide")?;
    project.add("cell", model.note()
        .field("front", Content::sequence([Content::text("Cell "), image.image()]))
        .field("back", sound.sound()))?;
    let output = project.build(BuildOptions::to("media-guide.apkg"))?;
    assert_eq!(output.report().counts().media, 3);
    Ok(())
}
```

类型化的 `image()` 和 `sound()` 值会保留依赖直至导出。手写 HTML、CSS 或脚本引用需要 `builder.asset(media)` 或 `project.add_asset(media)`；库不会从任意字符串推断文件内容。即使没有可被静态识别的引用，显式资源仍会被包含。

向 `with_export_name` 传入原始文件名。类型化声音引用在渲染时会转义 HTML 实体，因此 `tone&copy;.mp3` 仍引用该原名资源。不要预先转义文件名。声音文件名中的百分号和片段字符保持字面含义，并不是 URL 路径。

## 名称、MIME 与预算

默认导出名称由内容决定，与源路径无关。需要固定文件名时，应在创建引用前使用 `with_export_name`。重命名某个克隆不会改变之前的克隆或内容节点。

名称不能包含路径、控制字符或不可移植的保留名称。冲突检查使用 Unicode NFC 加大小写折叠：仅大小写或规范化形式不同也会冲突。名称与内容完全相同的重复操作具有幂等性；同名不同内容会失败，不留下部分注册状态。

包括扩展名在内的完整导出文件名最多为 255 个 UTF-8 字节。Project 与模板包的 JSON Schema 检查文件名语法和字符数；加载器还检查字节预算。例如，重复 128 次的 `é` 能通过 schema 字符限制，却占 256 字节，加载时返回 `MEDIA.EXPORT_NAME_INVALID`。构建前通过 `tools::load_project` 或 `NoteType::from_bundle` 校验完整输入。

MIME 语法必须与可识别的内容一致。原生字节没有 64 KiB 的内联限制。默认导入预算为每个资源 256 MiB；`file_with_limits` 和 `bytes_with_limits` 在读取前接收 `MediaLimits { max_bytes }`。大快照可能写入临时存储，并在最后一个所有者消失后清理。快照所有权不保证在源文件同时被修改的导入过程中获得原子的文件系统视图。

Project JSON 解码内联 `bytes` 数组时使用相同的默认单资源预算。遇到首个超限字节便停止，不再收集剩余数组，并保留带限制和已观察字节数的 `MediaError`。拒绝时的计数是下界，并非尚未读取数组的总大小。

有效的媒体包并不证明所有 Anki 客户端都能播放其编解码格式。请在目标客户端测试图片、声音和字体。参见[排查问题](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/zh-cn/docs/troubleshooting/#media-and-templates)。

### 类型化图片与声音的使用

构造函数保持不会失败。`Project::add` 检查导入时保留的 MIME：图片要求 `image/*`，声音引用接受 `audio/*` 和 `video/*`。`application/octet-stream`、文本、字体和 PDF 的类型化用法会返回 `NOTE.MEDIA_USAGE_INVALID`；用于原始 HTML/CSS 时应注册为显式资源。有效但未知的图片或视频 MIME 声明可以通过类别校验，但这并不认证解码器或播放器支持这些字节。重命名文件不会改变已保留的 MIME。构建仍会探测暂存字节并独立校验导出扩展名：名为 `wrong.mp3` 的 PNG 可以通过图片添加，却在构建时返回 `MEDIA.DECLARED_MIME_MISMATCH`。

## 批量媒体导入

这些方法已包含在公开 `0.3.1` 包中。

以受限并发导入一组文件，保持输入顺序，并保留拥有所有权的媒体快照供之后导出：

```rust
use ankiforge::Media;
let images = Media::files(["first.png", "second.png"])?;
```

Node 使用 `await Media.files(['first.png', 'second.png'])`；Python 使用 `Media.files(['first.png', 'second.png'])`。

### 批量行为与预算

Rust 使用 `Media::files(paths)`，Node 使用 `await Media.files(paths)`，Python 使用 `Media.files(paths)`，按输入顺序导入文件，每次调用最多四个工作线程。少于 16 个文件时串行运行。Rust 还提供 `files_with_limits`；Node 和 Python 接受与 `file` 相同的限制。限制按每个资源计算。若某项导入失败，调用会等待已启动的工作完成、释放此批次的快照，并返回输入顺序中的第一个错误。已有媒体所有者继续有效。Python 在导入期间释放 GIL；Node 在事件循环之外执行工作。单文件导入仍立即产生拥有所有权的快照；调用方必须选择批量方法才能获得导入并发。

存活快照共享进程级 **64 MiB** 内存预算。单个大于 1 MiB 的资源仍流式写入临时文件。编码媒体在每次预备处理中共享延迟分配的 **16 MiB** 缓冲池，池满后写入临时存储。这些预算不包含其他工作内存，也不是 RSS 上限；并发构建各自可以拥有编码池。

# Genera y actualiza mazos de Anki desde JSON

Canonical page: https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/es/docs/json-to-anki/
Language: es
Description: Lee JSON con Rust, Python o TypeScript, incluye imágenes y audio y revisa una actualización de APKG que solo cambia una respuesta.

Lee tres preguntas de biología desde JSON, añade una imagen y un fragmento de audio compartidos y exporta un APKG original junto con una actualización revisada que solo cambia una respuesta. Cada versión debe contener **3 notas, 3 tarjetas y 2 archivos multimedia**. Elige uno de los SDK siguientes; cada ejemplo es un programa completo. La exportación habitual no requiere instalar Anki.

Mantenimiento: responsables de Anki Forge · revisión del 2026-10-25.

## Archivos de entrada compartidos

Descarga [v1.json](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/v1.json), [v2.json](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/v2.json), [cell.png](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/cell.png) y [tone.wav](https://morehardy.github.io/anki-forge/generated/recipes/json-to-anki/tone.wav). La imagen es un diagrama de una célula; el audio es un tono breve generado, no una palabra pronunciada. En cada directorio nuevo de aplicación, coloca estos cuatro archivos en `recipe/`:

```text
json-deck/
  recipe/
    v1.json
    v2.json
    cell.png
    tone.wav
```

Ambos archivos JSON contienen `namespace`, `deck` y tres `notes` con valores persistentes de `id`, `front` y `back`. v2 solo cambia la primera respuesta. Tu aplicación analiza el JSON; Anki Forge se encarga de crear el contenido y generar el APKG. Si los datos no son de confianza, valida el esquema de tu aplicación antes de crear las notas.

## Rust

Rust 1.92 o posterior. El análisis de JSON usa `serde` y `serde_json`. Utiliza el paquete publicado de Anki Forge 0.3.1.

```sh
cargo new json-deck
cd json-deck
cargo add ankiforge@0.3.1
cargo add serde --features derive
cargo add serde_json
```

Guárdalo como `src/main.rs` y crea `recipe/` junto a `Cargo.toml`:

```rust
use ankiforge::update::CompareOptions;
use ankiforge::{BuildOptions, Content, Media, Note, Project};
use serde::Deserialize;
use std::{fs, path::Path};

#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct Dataset {
    namespace: String,
    deck: String,
    notes: Vec<Row>,
}

#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct Row {
    id: String,
    front: String,
    back: String,
}

fn project(input: &Path, version: &str) -> Result<Project, Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let data: Dataset = serde_json::from_slice(&fs::read(input.join(version))?)?;
    let image = Media::file(input.join("cell.png"))?;
    let audio = Media::file(input.join("tone.wav"))?;
    let mut project = Project::new(data.namespace)?.default_deck(data.deck);
    for row in data.notes {
        let front = Content::sequence([Content::text(row.front), image.image(), audio.sound()]);
        project.add(row.id, Note::basic(front, row.back))?;
    }
    Ok(project)
}

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let args: Vec<_> = std::env::args().collect();
    let input = Path::new(args.get(1).map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("recipe"));
    let output = Path::new(args.get(2).map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("output/rust"));
    fs::create_dir_all(output)?;
    let baseline = output.join("v1.apkg");
    let candidate = output.join("v2.apkg");
    if baseline.exists() || candidate.exists() {
        return Err("Choose a fresh output directory; keep original releases".into());
    }
    project(input, "v1.json")?.build(BuildOptions::to(&baseline))?;
    let next = project(input, "v2.json")?;
    let comparison = next.compare(CompareOptions::against(&baseline))?;
    fs::write(
        output.join("comparison.json"),
        serde_json::to_vec_pretty(&comparison.snapshot())?,
    )?;
    if !comparison.policy().allows_publication() {
        return Err("Comparison policy blocked publication; inspect comparison.json".into());
    }
    let prepared = next.prepare_publication(BuildOptions::to(&candidate).update_from(&baseline))?;
    let review = prepared
        .report()
        .comparison()
        .ok_or("Missing update comparison")?;
    fs::write(
        output.join("review.json"),
        serde_json::to_vec_pretty(&review.snapshot())?,
    )?;
    if !review.policy().allows_publication() {
        return Err("Prepared candidate blocked; inspect review.json".into());
    }
    let result = prepared.publish()?;
    println!("{}", result.artifact().path().display());
    Ok(())
}
```

```sh
cargo run -- recipe output/rust
```

## Python

CPython estándar 3.11 o posterior con un wheel para tu plataforma; las comprobaciones de publicación cubren las versiones 3.11–3.14. En Windows, activa el entorno con `.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1`. Utiliza el paquete publicado de Anki Forge 0.3.1.

